<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Mysuru: Heritage, Temples, and Dasara</title>
    <style>
        /* 
         * Mini Project CSS (50 Marks Quality)
         * Incorporates variables, flexbox, CSS grid, hover animations, and responsive design. 
         */
        :root {
            --primary-color: #8b0000; /* Heritage Maroon */
            --secondary-color: #d4af37; /* Royal Gold */
            --bg-light: #fdfbf7;
            --text-dark: #333;
        }
        
        * {
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
            box-sizing: border-box;
            font-family: 'Segoe UI', Tahoma, Geneva, Verdana, sans-serif;
        }

        body {
            background-color: var(--bg-light);
            color: var(--text-dark);
            line-height: 1.6;
        }

        /* Sticky Navigation Bar */
        nav {
            background-color: var(--primary-color);
            color: white;
            display: flex;
            justify-content: space-between;
            align-items: center;
            padding: 1rem 5%;
            position: sticky;
            top: 0;
            z-index: 1000;
            box-shadow: 0 4px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.2);
        }

        nav h1 {
            font-size: 1.8rem;
            color: var(--secondary-color);
            text-transform: uppercase;
            letter-spacing: 2px;
        }

        nav ul {
            list-style: none;
            display: flex;
            gap: 20px;
        }

        nav ul li a {
            color: white;
            text-decoration: none;
            font-weight: bold;
            transition: color 0.3s;
        }

        nav ul li a:hover {
            color: var(--secondary-color);
        }

        /* Hero Section with Parallax-like Background */
        .hero {
            /* Using a high-quality placeholder image for the palace/heritage theme */
            background: linear-gradient(rgba(139, 0, 0, 0.7), rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.7)), url('https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1600100397608-f010f41cb871?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=1920&q=80') center/cover;
            height: 60vh;
            display: flex;
            flex-direction: column;
            justify-content: center;
            align-items: center;
            text-align: center;
            color: white;
            padding: 0 20px;
        }

        .hero h2 {
            font-size: 3.5rem;
            color: var(--secondary-color);
            margin-bottom: 15px;
            text-shadow: 2px 2px 4px rgba(0,0,0,0.5);
        }

        .hero p {
            font-size: 1.2rem;
            max-width: 600px;
        }

        /* Main Container for Sections */
        .container {
            max-width: 1200px;
            margin: 0 auto;
            padding: 40px 20px;
        }

        /* Styled Section Titles */
        .section-title {
            text-align: center;
            font-size: 2.5rem;
            color: var(--primary-color);
            margin-bottom: 30px;
            position: relative;
        }

        .section-title::after {
            content: '';
            width: 80px;
            height: 4px;
            background-color: var(--secondary-color);
            display: block;
            margin: 10px auto 0;
        }

        /* CSS Grid Layout for Content Cards */
        .grid-container {
            display: grid;
            grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(300px, 1fr));
            gap: 30px;
            margin-bottom: 50px;
        }

        /* Card Styling & Hover Effects */
        .card {
            background: white;
            border-radius: 10px;
            overflow: hidden;
            box-shadow: 0 5px 15px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);
            transition: transform 0.3s ease, box-shadow 0.3s ease;
            border-bottom: 4px solid var(--secondary-color);
        }

        .card:hover {
            transform: translateY(-10px);
            box-shadow: 0 8px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.2);
        }

        .card-content {
            padding: 25px;
        }

        .card-title {
            color: var(--primary-color);
            font-size: 1.5rem;
            margin-bottom: 15px;
        }

        /* Current News/Highlight Box */
        .highlight-text {
            background-color: #fff8e1;
            padding: 20px;
            border-left: 6px solid var(--secondary-color);
            border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0;
            margin: 20px 0 40px 0;
            font-style: italic;
            box-shadow: 0 2px 5px rgba(0,0,0,0.05);
        }

        /* Footer */
        footer {
            background-color: #222;
            color: white;
            text-align: center;
            padding: 30px 20px;
            margin-top: 40px;
            border-top: 5px solid var(--secondary-color);
        }

        footer h2 {
            color: var(--secondary-color);
            margin-bottom: 10px;
            font-size: 1.5rem;
        }

        footer p {
            margin: 5px 0;
            color: #aaa;
            font-size: 0.9rem;
        }

        /* Mobile Responsiveness */
        @media (max-width: 768px) {
            nav {
                flex-direction: column;
                gap: 15px;
            }
            .hero h2 {
                font-size: 2.5rem;
            }
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

    <!-- Navigation Bar -->
    <nav>
        <h1>Mysuru Culture</h1>
        <ul>
            <li><a href="#home">Home</a></li>
            <li><a href="#temples">Temples</a></li>
            <li><a href="#dasara">Dasara Festival</a></li>
        </ul>
    </nav>

    <!-- Hero Banner -->
    <header id="home" class="hero">
        <h2>The Heritage City</h2>
        <p>Explore the magnificent traditions, historic architectural wonders, and the world-renowned Dasara festival of Mysuru.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="container">
        
        <!-- Temples Section -->
        <section id="temples">
            <h2 class="section-title">Sacred Temples of Mysuru</h2>
            
            <div class="grid-container">
                <!-- Chamundeshwari Card -->
                <div class="card">
                    <div class="card-content">
                        <h3 class="card-title">Chamundeshwari Temple</h3>
                        <p>Located atop the Chamundi Hills at an elevation of 3,300 ft, this historic Dravidian-style shrine is dedicated to Goddess Chamundeshwari. Visitors can climb the 1,008 stone steps constructed in 1659, encountering a colossal 15-foot Nandi statue at the 700th step. The temple serves as a central hub during Navratri.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Nanjangud Card -->
                <div class="card">
                    <div class="card-content">
                        <h3 class="card-title">Srikanteshwara Temple</h3>
                        <p>Situated in nearby Nanjangud (often called the "Dakshina Kashi"), this massive ancient temple is dedicated to Lord Shiva. Situated on the banks of the Kapila river, the complex features a massive gopuram, extensive pillared halls, and centuries-old stone carvings.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Somnathpur Card -->
                <div class="card">
                    <div class="card-content">
                        <h3 class="card-title">Chennakesava Temple</h3>
                        <p>Located in Somanathapura, this breathtaking 13th-century Hoysala temple is famed for its distinctive star-shaped platform and symmetrical architecture. It is a UNESCO World Heritage site where every inch of the outer walls features intricate soapstone carvings.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Dasara Section -->
        <section id="dasara">
            <h2 class="section-title">Mysuru Dasara (Nada Habba)</h2>
            
            <!-- Latest 2026 Information embedded into the project -->
            <div class="highlight-text">
                <p><strong>Recent Update:</strong> The grand Mysuru Dasara festivities concluded successfully in October 2026. A major highlight was the Vijayadashami Jamboo Savari, where the highly-trained elephant Prashantha successfully carried the iconic 750-kg Golden Howdah during the royal procession.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="grid-container">
                <!-- Dasara History -->
                <div class="card">
                    <div class="card-content">
                        <h3 class="card-title">History & Tradition</h3>
                        <p>Mysuru Dasara is a 10-day state festival (Nada Habba) celebrating the triumph of good over evil—specifically Goddess Chamundeshwari's victory over the demon Mahishasura. The Wadiyar royal family has maintained these grand traditions for centuries, merging royal pageantry with religious devotion.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Jamboo Savari -->
                <div class="card">
                    <div class="card-content">
                        <h3 class="card-title">The Jamboo Savari</h3>
                        <p>On the final day, Vijayadashami, the traditional Jamboo Savari (elephant procession) winds its way from the Mysore Palace to Bannimantap. The lead elephant carries the idol of Goddess Chamundeshwari in the revered Golden Ambari (Howdah).</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Palace Illumination -->
                <div class="card">
                    <div class="card-content">
                        <h3 class="card-title">Palace Illumination</h3>
                        <p>During the 10-day festival, the iconic Amba Vilas Palace is illuminated with nearly 100,000 light bulbs every evening. The festival also features an expansive cultural exhibition, a thrilling Torchlight Parade, and various classical music performances.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

    </div>

    <!-- Project Footer -->
    <footer>
        <h2>Web Development Mini Project</h2>
        <p>Topic: Mysuru Temple Information & Dasara Festival</p>
        <p>&copy; 2026 Academic Project Submission | Designed for 50 Marks</p>
    </footer>

</body>
</html>
